---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Phone Holder"
  category="Project | Product Development & Entrepreneurship"
  year="2024"
  description="IUT Figeac collaborative project combining mechanical product design, industrialisation, market analysis and business development around a custom phone-holder concept."
>

  <p slot="intro">
    A collaborative product-development project created at IUT Figeac,
    combining mechanical engineering, industrial feasibility and entrepreneurship
    around a custom phone-holder concept designed for corporate gifting.
  </p>


  <!-- PROJECT SNAPSHOT -->

  <section class="portfolio-hero">

    <div class="portfolio-outcome">

      <span class="portfolio-kicker">
        Outcome
      </span>

      <h2>
        From a mechanical idea to a complete product concept.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project went beyond designing a phone holder.
        We approached it as a complete product-development exercise,
        including technical design, industrial feasibility, market positioning
        and commercial strategy.
      </p>

      <div class="portfolio-metrics">

        <div>
          <strong>Product</strong>
          <span>Mechanical design</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>Market</strong>
          <span>Commercial study</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>IP</strong>
          <span>Patent-oriented work</span>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>


    <figure class="portfolio-main-visual">

      <img
        src="/images/projects/phone-holder/phone-holder-main.jpg"
        alt="Custom phone holder product developed at IUT Figeac"
      />

      <figcaption>
        Product concept | Customisable phone holder for corporate gifting
      </figcaption>

    </figure>

  </section>


  <!-- 01 | CONTEXT -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      01
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Context
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project was developed as part of a collaborative SAE project
        during my studies at IUT Figeac.
      </p>

      <p>
        The objective was to develop a phone-holder product while considering
        not only its mechanical design, but also the industrial and commercial
        conditions required to bring it to market.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 02 | PRODUCT IDEA -->

  <section class="portfolio-visual-section">

    <div class="portfolio-section-header">

      <span>
        02 | Product idea
      </span>

      <h2>
        Designing for both function and market.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="process-grid">

      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/initial-sketch.jpg"
          alt="Initial sketch of the phone holder"
        />

        <figcaption>
          01 | Initial concept
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/cad-concept.jpg"
          alt="CAD model of the phone holder"
        />

        <figcaption>
          02 | Product development
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/product-visual.jpg"
          alt="Final phone holder product concept"
        />

        <figcaption>
          03 | Product positioning
        </figcaption>

      </figure>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 03 | OBJECTIVES -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      03
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Project objectives
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Develop a functional phone-holder product
        </li>

        <li>
          Create a concept suitable for customisation
        </li>

        <li>
          Evaluate industrial feasibility
        </li>

        <li>
          Study potential market demand
        </li>

        <li>
          Define a commercial positioning
        </li>

        <li>
          Explore intellectual-property protection
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 04 | MY CONTRIBUTION -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      04
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        My contribution
      </h2>

      <p>
        My role extended across both the engineering and business sides of the project.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Coordinated project activities within the team
        </li>

        <li>
          Contributed to the product-development strategy
        </li>

        <li>
          Worked on market analysis
        </li>

        <li>
          Participated in industrial and commercial studies
        </li>

        <li>
          Contributed to business-development strategy
        </li>

        <li>
          Worked on intellectual-property considerations
        </li>

        <li>
          Participated in patent drafting
        </li>

        <li>
          Prepared a letter of intent
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 05 | PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT -->

  <section class="portfolio-system">

    <div class="portfolio-section-header">

      <span>
        05 | Product development
      </span>

      <h2>
        Engineering a simple product seriously.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="system-grid">

      <figure class="system-overview">

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/product-overview.jpg"
          alt="Overall phone holder product architecture"
        />

        <figcaption>
          Product architecture
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <div class="subsystem-stack">

        <figure>

          <img
            src="/images/projects/phone-holder/detail.jpg"
            alt="Detailed view of the phone holder"
          />

          <figcaption>
            Product detail | Geometry and user interaction
          </figcaption>

        </figure>


        <div class="subsystem-copy">

          <h3>
            Design logic
          </h3>

          <p>
            Even a relatively simple consumer product requires balancing
            functionality, usability, manufacturability and cost.
          </p>

          <p>
            The project therefore treated the phone holder as a complete product
            rather than only as a CAD exercise.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 06 | MARKET STUDY -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      06
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Market study
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project included a market-analysis phase to understand potential
        customers, competing products and positioning opportunities.
      </p>

      <p>
        Particular attention was given to the possibility of using the product
        as a customisable corporate gift.
      </p>

      <p>
        This required connecting product characteristics with a concrete
        commercial use case rather than designing without a defined market.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 07 | INDUSTRIAL STUDY -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      07
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Industrial feasibility
      </h2>

      <p>
        The product also had to be considered from an industrial perspective.
      </p>

      <p>
        The objective was to determine whether the concept could realistically
        move from prototype to repeatable production while remaining economically
        coherent.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Manufacturing feasibility
        </li>

        <li>
          Production repeatability
        </li>

        <li>
          Product customisation
        </li>

        <li>
          Cost considerations
        </li>

        <li>
          Industrial scalability
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 08 | ENTREPRENEURSHIP -->

  <section class="portfolio-wide-visual">

    <figure>

      <img
        src="/images/projects/phone-holder/business-model.jpg"
        alt="Product and business-development structure for the phone holder project"
      />

      <figcaption>
        Product development | Engineering, industrialisation and business strategy
      </figcaption>

    </figure>

  </section>


  <!-- 09 | COMMERCIAL STRATEGY -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      09
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Commercial strategy
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project required developing a business-development approach around
        the product.
      </p>

      <p>
        This included studying how the phone holder could be positioned,
        personalised and presented to potential corporate customers.
      </p>

      <p>
        A letter of intent was also prepared as part of the commercial-development
        process.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 10 | INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      10
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Intellectual property
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project also introduced the question of how a product concept can
        be protected before commercialisation.
      </p>

      <p>
        I participated in work related to intellectual property and patent drafting,
        which provided an initial understanding of the relationship between
        engineering design and legal protection of technical concepts.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 11 | DEVELOPMENT PROCESS -->

  <section class="portfolio-visual-section">

    <div class="portfolio-section-header">

      <span>
        11 | Development
      </span>

      <h2>
        Idea. Product. Market. Business.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="process-grid">

      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/design-phase.jpg"
          alt="Phone holder design phase"
        />

        <figcaption>
          Design
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/industrial-study.jpg"
          alt="Industrial study for the phone holder project"
        />

        <figcaption>
          Industrialisation
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/phone-holder/market-study.jpg"
          alt="Market study for the phone holder project"
        />

        <figcaption>
          Market development
        </figcaption>

      </figure>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 12 | DOCUMENTATION -->

  <section class="portfolio-documents">

    <div class="portfolio-section-header">

      <span>
        12 | Documentation
      </span>

      <h2>
        Project records.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="document-grid">

      <a
        href="/documents/phone-holder/project-report.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        class="document-card"
      >

        <div>

          <span class="document-type">
            PDF
          </span>

          <h3>
            Project report
          </h3>

          <p>
            Product development, technical choices and project methodology.
          </p>

        </div>

        <span class="document-arrow">
          ↗
        </span>

      </a>


      <a
        href="/documents/phone-holder/market-study.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        class="document-card"
      >

        <div>

          <span class="document-type">
            PDF
          </span>

          <h3>
            Market study
          </h3>

          <p>
            Market analysis, product positioning and commercial opportunities.
          </p>

        </div>

        <span class="document-arrow">
          ↗
        </span>

      </a>


      <a
        href="/documents/phone-holder/ip-study.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        class="document-card"
      >

        <div>

          <span class="document-type">
            PDF
          </span>

          <h3>
            IP study
          </h3>

          <p>
            Intellectual-property work and patent-oriented documentation.
          </p>

        </div>

        <span class="document-arrow">
          ↗
        </span>

      </a>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 13 | SKILLS -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      13
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Skills developed
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Product development
        </li>

        <li>
          Mechanical design
        </li>

        <li>
          Industrial feasibility analysis
        </li>

        <li>
          Market analysis
        </li>

        <li>
          Business development
        </li>

        <li>
          Project coordination
        </li>

        <li>
          Intellectual property
        </li>

        <li>
          Technical entrepreneurship
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 14 | LEARNING -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      14
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        What I learned
      </h2>

      <p>
        The Phone Holder project was one of my first opportunities to consider
        engineering from an entrepreneurial perspective.
      </p>

      <p>
        It showed me that a technically functional product is only one part of
        a successful development process.
      </p>

      <p>
        Manufacturing feasibility, market demand, commercial positioning and
        intellectual property can be just as important as the mechanical design itself.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>

</ProjectLayout>